# AutoHotkey Runtime Workflow

When working on `.ahk` files in this repo:

- Treat the compiled `.exe` as the primary runtime target.
- Do not leave both the script interpreter (`AutoHotkey.exe` running `.ahk`) and compiled `.exe` running at the same time.
- After substantive `.ahk` edits, compile to `autoswitch mic for VR.exe` using the repo icon at `images/beyond_nvidia.ico`.
- After every compile, copy the `.exe` to `C:\Users\HeavyGee\Documents\AutoHotkey\autoswitch mic for VR.exe`.
- Run the app from `C:\Users\HeavyGee\Documents\AutoHotkey` after compile/copy. Do not run the repo copy directly.
- If a matching `.ahk` interpreter instance is running for the same script, stop only that matching interpreter process before relaunching `.exe`.
- Do not kill unrelated AutoHotkey scripts.

## Preferred Behavior

- `autoswitch mic for VR.ahk` -> compile with `images/beyond_nvidia.ico` -> copy exe to `C:\Users\HeavyGee\Documents\AutoHotkey` -> run from there
- If both tray icons exist (script + exe), keep only the `.exe` instance.
